CHAPTER.VERS:
And when he came to the king, the king said to him, Micaiah, shall we go to Ramoth-gilead to battle, or shall I forbear? And he said, Go

          {+}
         up, and prosper; and they will be delivered into your

          {+}
         hand.

And [Micaiah] said, Therefore hear

          {+}
         the word of Yahweh: I saw Yahweh sitting on his throne, and all the host of heaven standing on his right hand and on his left.

And the king of Israel said, Take

          {+}
         Micaiah, and carry him back to Amon the governor of the city, and to Joash the king's son;

And Micaiah said, If you return at all in peace, Yahweh has not spoken by me. And he said, Hear, you

          {+}
         peoples, all of you

          {+}
        .
